{
  "_about": "The whole-number knob grammar every lane shares (RAINCLOUD_ROW_GROUP_*, and every count knob in raincloud/pipeline/spec.py). Read by pytest (tests/test_native_protocol.py), cargo test (sidecars/rust/src/lib.rs) and JUnit (KnobsTest, sidecars/java/conformance-common), so a grammar change is declared here once. After trimming ASCII whitespace (space, \\t, \\n, \\r, \\v, \\f): empty or zero disables the knob (value null); otherwise the value must match ^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$ and is truncated toward zero. `error` is a substring of every lane's message. An unset knob is its default, and a value that is not UTF-8 is an error naming the variable; neither can be written in this file.",
